      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses this high greatly raise the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit mix-up? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg three times daily** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, split into divided doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also add a note with your rationale to the order."
      }
     ],
